1
00:00:00,489 --> 00:00:09,248
(Q11（table横纵表格填空）) Hello, I'm delighted to welcome you to our Wildlife Club, and very pleased that you're interested in the countryside and the plants and creatures of this area.

2
00:00:09,248 --> 00:00:15,576
I think you'll be surprised at the variety we have here, even though we're not far from London.

3
00:00:15,576 --> 00:00:20,455
I'll start by telling you about some of the parks and open spaces nearby.

4
00:00:20,455 --> 00:00:24,409
One very pleasant place is Halland Common.

5
00:00:24,409 --> 00:00:36,933
This has been public land for hundreds of years, and what you'll find interesting is that the River Ouse, which flows into the sea eighty kilometres away, has its source in the common.

6
00:00:36,933 --> 00:00:46,575
There's an information board about the plants and animals you can see here, and by the way, the common is accessible 24 hours a day.

7
00:00:46,575 --> 00:00:51,934
(Q12) Then there's Holt Island, which is noted for its great range of trees.

8
00:00:51,934 --> 00:01:01,512
In the past willows were grown here commercially for basket-making, and this ancient craft has recently been reintroduced.

9
00:01:01,512 --> 00:01:12,628
The island is only open to the public from Friday to Sunday, because it's quite small, and if there were people around every day, much of the wildlife would keep away.

10
00:01:12,628 --> 00:01:18,183
(Q13) From there it's just a short walk across the bridge to Longfield Country Park.

11
00:01:18,183 --> 00:01:23,472
Longfield has a modern replica of a farm from over two thousand years ago.&nbsp;

12
00:01:23,472 --> 00:01:29,559
Children's activities are often arranged there, like bread-making and face-painting.

13
00:01:29,559 --> 00:01:36,307
The park is only open during daylight hours, so bear that in mind if you decide to go there.

14
00:01:36,307 --> 00:01:45,069
(Q14（单选）) Longfield Park has a programme of activities throughout the year, and to give you a sample, this is what's happening in the next few days.&nbsp;

15
00:01:45,069 --> 00:01:51,103
On Monday you can learn about herbs, and how they've been used over the centuries.

16
00:01:51,103 --> 00:01:58,257
You'll start with a tour of our herb garden, practise the technique of using them as colour dyes for cloth.

17
00:01:58,257 --> 00:02:04,680
And listen to an illustrated talk about their use in cooking and medicine.

18
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:12,487
(Q15) Then on Wednesday you can join local experts to discover the variety of insects and birds that appear in the evening.

19
00:02:12,487 --> 00:02:20,975
We keep to a small number of people in the group, so if you want to go you'll need to phone the park ranger a few days ahead.

20
00:02:20,975 --> 00:02:25,529
There's a small charge, which you should pay when you turn up.

21
00:02:25,529 --> 00:02:34,174
(Q16) I'm sure you're all keen to help with the practical task of looking after the park, so on Saturday you can join a working party.

22
00:02:34,174 --> 00:02:44,140
You'll have a choice of all sorts of activities, from planting hedges to picking up litter so you'll be able to change from one to another when you feel like it.

23
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:51,678
The rangers will be hard at work all day, but do come and join in, even for just a short while.

24
00:02:51,678 --> 00:02:58,657
One thing, though, is to make sure you're wearing something that you don't mind getting dirty or torn.

25
00:02:58,657 --> 00:03:08,117
(Q17（地图题）) And finally I'd like to tell you about our new wildlife area, Hinchingbrooke Park, which will be opened to the public next month.

26
00:03:08,117 --> 00:03:17,021
This slide doesn't really indicate how big it is, but anyway, you can see the two gates into the park, and the main paths.

27
00:03:17,021 --> 00:03:24,589
As you can see, there's a lake in the north west of the park, with a bird hide to the west of it, at the end of a path.

28
00:03:24,589 --> 00:03:29,883
So it'll be a nice quiet place for watching the birds on the lake.

29
00:03:29,883 --> 00:03:38,456
(Q18) Fairly close to where refreshments are available, there's a dog-walking area in the southern part of the park, leading off from the path.

30
00:03:38,456 --> 00:03:47,318
(Q19) And if you just want to sit and relax, you can go to the flower garden; that's the circular area on the map surrounded by paths.

31
00:03:47,318 --> 00:03:53,844
(Q20) And finally, there's a wooded area in the western section of the park, between two paths.

32
00:03:53,844 --> 00:03:56,344
Okay, that's enough from me, so let's go on to…

